// TEST: Idx Card Static Bound Key Order
// ============================================================================
// THE CONSUMPTION-PATH twin of structs/050, under ADVERSARIAL KEY ORDER.
//
// `let static a_card = idx_card(Ranged)` names `idx_card` and `Ranged` and no
// static at all, yet folding it requires `zz_hi` — the bound of a field of the
// type it names. The dependency edge is learned from the TYPE, by pulling in
// the statics its field bounds and declared conjuncts name. Missing that edge
// is the bug this family exists to catch.
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS ALONGSIDE index-types/146. Two reasons, both about the
// pin being real rather than lucky:
//
//  1. KEY ORDER, NOT SOURCE ORDER, IS WHAT EXERCISES THE EDGE. Static
//     resolution drains a Map in KEY order, so a missing edge is invisible
//     whenever the depended-on static sorts before its consumer — the
//     resolver stumbles into the right order and the test passes with the
//     edge logic deleted. index-types/146 happens to be adversarial (its
//     consumer `CARD2` sorts before `LO`), but only by accident of naming,
//     and any future rename would silently gut it. Here it is deliberate and
//     documented: `a_card` sorts before `zz_hi` under every comparer, so
//     without the edge the fold is attempted first and dies on "undefined
//     variable 'zz_hi'".
//  2. THE TWO SEEDS ARE INDEPENDENT. The struct-LITERAL path (structs/050)
//     and this CONSUMPTION path are separate collection sites, so one can
//     regress while the other stays green. Pinning only one leaves half the
//     fix unguarded — which is exactly how this bug reached the tree the
//     first time, having been fixed on the path where it was noticed.
//
// DO NOT rename these bindings and do not move `zz_hi` upward. Both properties
// are invisible and both are the test.
//
// The count is deliberately trivial — `m` over the inclusive [0, 3] is 4 cells
// with no conjunct to filter them — because this file is about ORDERING, not
// counting. If the edge works, the number is uninteresting; if it does not,
// there is no number at all.
// ============================================================================
static struct Ranged {
    m: Int<min=0, max=zz_hi>
}

let static a_card = idx_card(Ranged)
// EXPECT: a_card = 4

let static zz_hi = 3
